%% RENDERING NOTES -- compiled by mermaid-cli via scripts/render_architecture.sh.
%% Three settings exist to survive that compiler rather than to taste:
%% -
%% htmlLabels: false. With HTML labels mermaid measures a subgraph title in one
%%   font and clips it in another, which produced "ENCODER", "UNCERTAINT" and
%%   "NOT BI" in earlier PNGs. SVG text is measured correctly. The cost is <b>
%%   and <br/>, so every label is a markdown string in backticks.
%% themeCSS. With htmlLabels off the theme font is not applied to SVG text and
%%   it falls back to serif. This forces it back.
%% No chains inside a grouping box. A subgraph's `direction` is IGNORED once an
%%   edge crosses its boundary, so an internal A --> B --> C costs three ranks
%%   whatever the direction says. Siblings land on one rank.
%% -
%% Also: a four-space indent after a blank line inside a label is a markdown
%% code block, which renders ** literally. Continuation lines are flush left.

